<title>AUSTRALIA: SOCCER-AUSTRALIA BEAT SOLOMON ISLANDS 6-2 IN W.CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-AUSTRALIA BEAT SOLOMON ISLANDS 6-2 IN W.CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia beat Solomon Islands</p>
<p>6-2 (halftime 3-1) in a World Cup Oceania zone group one</p>
<p>qualifying match at Parramatta Stadium on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Australia - Robbie Slater 16, Graham Arnold 17, Jimmy</p>
<p>Kaierea 39 own goal, Ernie Tapai 48, 52, Aurelio Vidmar 75</p>
<p>penalty</p>
<p>Solomon Islands - Augustine Peli 29, Batram Suri 66</p>
<p>    Standings	   P   W   D   L   F   A   Pts</p>
<p> Australia		3   3   0   0  24   2    9</p>
<p> Solomon Islands	3   1   0   2   6  20    3</p>
<p> Tahiti		   2   0   0   2   1   9    0</p>
<p>Next match: June 19, in Sydney, Tahiti v Australia</p>
</text>
